  faq:[["Is Kakobuy Finds the official Kakobuy website?","No. This is an independent discovery and education site. Kakobuy handles purchasing, warehouse operations, inspection options, parcel submission and international delivery."],["What does W2C mean?","W2C means “where to cop”—where to find or buy an item. A useful entry shows the source, preview, price context, last-check date and a path to Kakobuy."],["Are Kakobuy QC photos free?","Standard photos are included with the applicable inspection option. Personalized photos are listed at ¥2 each, while three parcel photos are free when selected."],["Can QC photos prove authenticity?","No. They can reveal visible color, quantity, labels, stitching and exterior defects, but cannot prove authenticity, hidden construction, electronics, materials or durability."],["Does Kakobuy charge a service fee?","Basic agent purchasing is listed without a service fee. Buyers still pay the item, domestic and international shipping, possible customs charges, payment processing and optional services."],["How is international shipping calculated?","It depends on destination, line, restrictions and billable weight. Carriers usually charge the greater of actual and volumetric weight."],["Is the ¥3000 new-user coupon cash?","No. It is a coupon bundle with minimum-spend, validity and shipping-use conditions, not unrestricted account credit."],["How often are product links checked?","The catalog prioritizes recently checked links, but marketplace listings can change or disappear. Review the final product page before payment."],["Why can two 5 kg parcels have different prices?","Dimensions, item attributes, destination, line eligibility, adjustments and volume divisors can differ. A bulky parcel may be billed at a higher weight."],["What should I check before buying a W2C find?","Confirm the marketplace, variation, size, availability, domestic shipping, return conditions and visual evidence. Do not rely on one promotional image."]],
